{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Code Quality Review on Save",
  "description": "Analyzes modified source code files for potential improvements when changes are saved. Reviews for code smells, design pattern opportunities, best practices, readability, maintainability, and performance optimizations while preserving existing functionality.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "*.java",
      "*.ts",
      "*.vue",
      "*.js"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Analyze the modified source code file for potential improvements. Focus on:\n\n1. **Code Smells**: Identify any anti-patterns, duplicated logic, overly complex methods, long parameter lists, or god classes.\n2. **Design Patterns**: Suggest applicable design patterns that could improve the code structure (e.g., Strategy, Factory, Observer).\n3. **Best Practices**: Check adherence to project coding standards — constructor injection, proper use of @Transactional, DTO patterns, validation annotations, i18n usage, and Composition API conventions.\n4. **Readability**: Flag unclear naming, missing or misleading comments, inconsistent formatting, or overly nested logic.\n5. **Maintainability**: Identify tight coupling, missing abstractions, or areas where the code could be more modular.\n6. **Performance**: Spot potential N+1 queries, unnecessary object creation, missing indexes hints, inefficient collection operations, or opportunities for caching.\n\nProvide concise, actionable suggestions. Do not suggest changes that would alter existing functionality. Prioritize the most impactful improvements."
  }
}